Subject: [PATCH] zink: texture transfers through the CPU on Qualcomm's proprietary driver

With PIPE_TEXTURE_TRANSFER_BLIT, the state tracker uploads a texture from a bound PBO with a draw
(st_pbo: a fragment shader that reads the PBO through a texel buffer and writes the texture).
D2GL uploads its movie frames that way. On Qualcomm's Adreno 650 driver (Vulkan 1.1.128, driver
0746.0, through Venus) the GPU then hangs at the first movie frames, every time: kgsl "GPU hang
detected", the same submission of the game's context each time, three faults in 3 s, a lost
device (VK_ERROR_DEVICE_LOST), and the game ends. With the draw-based PBO upload off, the
uploads go through _mesa_store_texsubimage (a CPU copy from the mapped PBO into the mapped
texture): the movie plays and PD2's menu runs.

Give that driver no blit- or compute-based texture transfers (PIPE_TEXTURE_TRANSFER_DEFAULT).
This also keeps ReadPixels and GetTexImage on their CPU paths there. Through Venus, Zink sees
the host's driver ID only when the host driver has VK_KHR_maintenance7; Qualcomm's Vulkan 1.1
driver has not, so Zink sees VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_VENUS, and the vendor ID stays the host's
(0x5143, Qualcomm): that pair counts too (this GL stack is used only through Venus; Turnip has
its own, newer Mesa). Only for the system-driver mode's older GL stack (Mesa 25.1.9,
build-sysdrv.sh).

---
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/zink/zink_screen.c
@@ -965,6 +965,15 @@
           screen->info.have_KHR_16bit_storage &&
           screen->info.have_KHR_shader_float16_int8)
          mode |= PIPE_TEXTURE_TRANSFER_COMPUTE;
+      /* Qualcomm's proprietary driver (also through Venus, which keeps the
+       * host's vendor ID 0x5143) hangs the GPU when the state tracker uploads
+       * a PBO with a draw (D2GL's movie frames): texture transfers go through
+       * the CPU there.
+       */
+      if (zink_driverid(screen) == VK_DRIVER_ID_QUALCOMM_PROPRIETARY ||
+          (zink_driverid(screen) == VK_DRIVER_ID_MESA_VENUS &&
+           screen->info.props.vendorID == 0x5143))
+         mode = PIPE_TEXTURE_TRANSFER_DEFAULT;
       caps->texture_transfer_modes = mode;
    }
 
